{
  "type": "plugin-workflow-eval",
  "plugin_name": "deft-aoi-loop-plugin",
  "plugin_source": ".",
  "skills_dir": [
    "applications/workflow-deft-aoi-loop",
    "data/deft-aoi-rca-changenet",
    "data/deft-aoi-anomalygen-inference",
    "data/deft-aoi-omniverse-sdg",
    "data/deft-aoi-data-mining"
  ],
  "orchestrator_skill": "applications/workflow-deft-aoi-loop",
  "evals": [
    {
      "id": "deft-loop-sdg-mining",
      "prompt": "Run the DEFT Loop end-to-end as a smoke test on subset data with 2 augmentation arms enabled (Omniverse SDG + Data Mining). Skip AnomalyGen.\n\n## Plugin Installation\nThis eval depends on the `deft-aoi-loop-plugin` plugin (bundled in the `tao-skills-external` repo). Before starting, install the plugin fresh so the orchestrator + all sub-skills are on the Claude Code load path:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Locate the tao-skills-external repo root (this is the plugin marketplace root)\nPLUGIN_ROOT=\"${{CI_PROJECT_DIR:-$HOME/tao-skills-external}}\"\n\n# 2. Clear any cached install\nrm -rf ~/.claude/plugins/cache/tao-skill-bank/deft-aoi-loop-plugin\n```\n\nThen run the install slash-commands inside the Claude Code session:\n```\n/plugin marketplace add $PLUGIN_ROOT\n/plugin install deft-aoi-loop-plugin@tao-skill-bank\n/plugin marketplace update tao-skill-bank\n```\n\n## Skill\nUse the `workflow-deft-aoi-loop` skill as the orchestrator \u2014 it drives the full DEFT loop end-to-end and invokes its sub-skills by name:\n- `deft-aoi-rca-changenet` \u2014 root cause analysis on baseline inference\n- `deft-aoi-anomalygen-inference` \u2014 Arm A (diffusion-based defect inpainting)\n- `deft-aoi-omniverse-sdg` \u2014 Arm B (physics-based ray-traced paired SDG)\n- `deft-aoi-data-mining` \u2014 Arm C (k-NN retrieval from mining pool)\n\nLet the orchestrator drive \u2014 do not run sub-skills directly.\n\n## Environment (omnistation, airgapped)\nThis box cannot reach huggingface.co or pull from `nvcr.io/nvidian/iva/*` directly. All required artifacts are pre-staged. Pre-flight setup is documented at `reference-workflows/deft-loop/.ci/airgap.md`. Do not download anything from S3 during the run.\n\nWhat is already on the box:\n- `~/workspace/` \u2014 symlink to `~/deft_loop_subset_data/` (subset of validation images, base training CSV, USD scene, mining source pool, backbone).\n- Docker images already loaded: `nvcr.io/nvidia/tao/tao-toolkit:6.26.3-pyt`, `nvcr.io/nvidian/iva/embed:latest`, `nvcr.io/nvidian/iva/mining:latest`, `nvcr.io/nvidian/iva/pcb-aoi-ov-sdg:pair-feature`.\n- nvidia-container-toolkit installed; Docker `--gpus all` works without sudo; `sudo` is configured NOPASSWD.\n- Python venv at `/opt/skill-eval-venv/bin/python` with pandas + pyarrow (use it for parquet ops). PIL is NOT installed in this venv.\n- SigLIP HF cache pre-staged at `~/hf_models/siglip-hf-cache/` for Arm C (no `HF_TOKEN` needed at runtime).\n\n## HF model paths (all local, do not download)\n\n```\n~/hf_models/\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 siglip-hf-cache/                    # for Arm C (Data Mining) \u2014 proper HF cache structure\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 hub/models--google--siglip-base-patch16-224/\n        \u251c\u2500\u2500 snapshots/<hash>/{{config.json, model.safetensors, spiece.model, ...}}\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500 refs/main\n```\n\nEmbed container (for Data Mining target embeddings):\n```\ndocker run ... \\\n  -v $HOME/hf_models/siglip-hf-cache:/data/workspace/hf_cache \\\n  -v <mining_workspace>:/data/workspace_outputs \\\n  -v <mining_workspace>/targets:/data/target \\\n  -e HF_HOME=/data/workspace/hf_cache \\\n  -e TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=1 -e HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 \\\n  --name embed-worker --gpus all --ipc=host --entrypoint sh \\\n  nvcr.io/nvidian/iva/embed:latest -c \"tail -f /dev/null\"\n```\n\nWhen invoking `image_embeddings.py` inside the embed container, pass `--model_path google/siglip-base-patch16-224` (the HF repo id). Transformers will resolve it from the offline cache via `HF_HOME`.\n\n## DEFT loop parameters\n- KPI target: `FAR < 0.1% at Recall = 100%`\n- Max iterations: 1\n- Training epochs: 2 per iteration\n- Baseline checkpoint: none \u2014 train from scratch\n- Workspace: `~/workspace`\n\n## Dataset paths (relative to workspace)\n- Training CSV: `train/base/train_combined_clean_keep_pass_1pct_keep_non_pass_1pct.csv` (210 rows)\n- Validation CSV: `kpi/valid_combined_clean_keep_pass_1pct_keep_non_pass_100pct.csv` (249 rows)\n- Images root: `kpi/images/`\n- Spec YAML: `specs/baseline_spec.yaml`\n- Backbone: `augmentation/backbone/C-RADIOv2_B.pth`\n\n## Augmentation arms \u2014 Arm B + Arm C ENABLED, Arm A SKIPPED\n\nArm A \u2014 AnomalyGen: SKIP. Do not run this arm. Document the skip in the iteration summary and continue.\n\nArm B \u2014 Omniverse SDG:\n- Docker image: `nvcr.io/nvidian/iva/pcb-aoi-ov-sdg:pair-feature`.\n- USD scene: mount `~/workspace/augmentation/omniverse/scene/dgx-spark-P4242-A04/temp_scene.usd` into the container and override `scene:` in the config to the mounted path.\n- Defect types: agent selects from RCA output (shift / tombstone / sideflip / missing). For the CI smoke test, prioritise the one or two highest-impact defect types rather than all four.\n- num_triggers: 1 (smoke test).\n- Budget at least 60 min wall time for the SDG container on L40S; do not enforce a shorter timeout.\n\nArm C \u2014 Data Mining:\n- Source parquet: `~/workspace/augmentation/mining/mining0330_defect_embeddings.parquet`\n- Source images: `~/workspace/augmentation/mining/` (`defect/` and `golden/` are direct children)\n- Desired count: 20 (k-NN cosine; filter the result to files that exist locally \u2014 the subset trims the source pool)\n\n## Execution discipline \u2014 avoid runaway loops\n\nThe eval values end-to-end completion of the full DEFT loop over perfection of any single arm. Apply these bounds up front:\n\n- **Retry budget:** at most 5 retry attempts per sub-step. After 5 unsuccessful retries of the same action, record the failure in the transcript and move on. Do not enter a debug loop chasing one error for more than a handful of attempts.\n- **Arm time-box:** if a single arm has not produced its expected output within ~75 minutes of wall time, stop it gracefully, record what went wrong in the transcript, and proceed with whatever outputs other arms produced. Partial results + a clean stop are more valuable than an unbounded retry loop.\n- **Background work verification:** if you launch a container in the background, plan the verification checkpoint up front. `docker ps` status alone is not proof of progress (some containers keep their parent process alive even after the inner script has crashed). Always inspect logs and output-file counts before declaring a background arm complete, and pipe container logs to a file so evidence survives even if the container is later removed.\n- **When in doubt, record and move on.** The grader values a transcript that honestly logs partial failures over one that spends the whole time on a single obstacle.\n\n## Artifacts to upload (save under {artifacts_dir})\nDo NOT upload model checkpoint files. Cherry-pick these for the MR:\n\n**KPI / metrics:**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_summary.md` \u2190 `~/workspace/results/<run>/baseline_summary.md`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_summary.md` \u2190 `~/workspace/results/<run>/iter1_summary.md`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/DEFT_Loop_Report.md` \u2190 `~/workspace/results/<run>/DEFT_Loop_Report.md`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/deft_state.json` \u2190 `~/workspace/results/<run>/deft_state.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_inference_summary.txt` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/inference/summary.txt`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_inference_summary.txt` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/inference/summary.txt`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_threshold_metrics.csv` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/inference/threshold_metrics.csv`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_threshold_metrics.csv` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/inference/threshold_metrics.csv`\n\n**Visualizations (PNGs from `analyze_kpi.py`):**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_score_distribution.png` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/inference/score_distribution_with_recall_100_threshold.png`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_confusion_matrix.png` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/inference/confusion_matrix_recall_100.png`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_score_distribution.png` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/inference/score_distribution_with_recall_100_threshold.png`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_confusion_matrix.png` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/inference/confusion_matrix_recall_100.png`\n\n**Sample augmented images (3 of each, picked at random):**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/omniverse_sdg_samples/` \u2190 3 golden + 3 defect sample pairs from Arm B output\n- `{artifacts_dir}/mining_samples/` \u2190 3 defect + 3 golden files referenced by `<run>/iter1/mining_output/mined_similar_files.csv`\n\n**RCA report:**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_RCA_report.md` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/rca_results/<timestamp>/RCA_Report.md` (or `rca_summary.json` if no full report exists)\n\n## Pipeline Execution granularity for this eval\nWhen rendering the Pipeline Execution table in your Step 3 summary, use EXACTLY these rows (one row per logical stage \u2014 do NOT unfold internal sub-steps into separate rows):\n\n1. `Baseline Training` \u2014 2-epoch ChangeNet train from scratch on the base CSV.\n2. `Baseline Inference + KPI` \u2014 inference on the KPI validation set + `analyze_kpi.py`.\n3. `Baseline RCA` \u2014 `rca-changenet` run on the baseline results.\n4. `Arm A \u2014 AnomalyGen` \u2014 one row showing SKIPPED.\n5. `Arm B \u2014 Omniverse SDG` \u2014 the entire Omniverse SDG arm as ONE row.\n6. `Arm C \u2014 Data Mining` \u2014 embed targets + mine + copy, all in ONE row.\n7. `Data Merge` \u2014 merge of base CSV + Arm B + Arm C outputs into the iter1 training CSV.\n8. `Iter1 Training` \u2014 2-epoch ChangeNet train on the merged CSV.\n9. `Iter1 Inference + KPI` \u2014 inference + `analyze_kpi.py` on iter1 checkpoint.\n\nTypical columns: `Stage | Duration | Key Output / Metric`. Keep it to these 9 rows.\n\n## Expected outcome\nThe entire DEFT loop runs autonomously without human intervention. **KPI magnitude is not graded** \u2014 the only grading criterion is end-to-end completion. The final `deft_state.json` should show `iterations.iter1.status == 'complete'` and the report should list Arm B and Arm C as enabled with non-zero augmented-image counts, and Arm A as skipped.",
      "expected_outcome": "Full DEFT loop completes end-to-end with: (1) `deft_state.json` showing `iterations.iter1.status == 'complete'`; (2) `DEFT_Loop_Report.md` written; (3) baseline + iter1 inference CSVs and KPI summaries present; (4) Arm B (Omniverse SDG) produces paired images; (5) Arm C (Data Mining) produces `mined_similar_files.csv` with at least one entry; (6) Arm A (AnomalyGen) explicitly logged as SKIPPED; (7) the iter1 training CSV merges rows from Arm B + Arm C; (8) all required artifacts listed in the prompt are present under {artifacts_dir}. KPI magnitude is NOT graded."
    }
  ],
  "credentials": [],
  "_note": "SLOW MANUAL EVAL \u2014 CI does NOT read this file (only `eval.config` at this path is CI-consumed). Run manually via `test_local.py` / `test_skill.py` when validating the SDG arm."
}
